{
  "_comment": "Editing a selection by voice (SelectionCommand), shared by the macOS and Windows tests so both apps agree. replies: a model's output (after Prompts.sanitizeCommandOutput) for a selection, read as a rewrite or as an answer to a question (SelectionCommand.reply), and whether Prompts.commandFallback lets it go over the selection (expectFallback null) or not. sanitize: what Prompts.sanitizeCommandOutput takes out of a model's output for a selection (preambles, notes, fences, quotes, tags) and what it leaves because the selection has it too. blocks: how Prompts.commandBlock keeps a selection (or an instruction) from spelling the request's own tags, changing nothing else. apps: how the app a selection is in is read (SelectionApp): terminals are refused, and line-copy editors are only read through Accessibility / UI Automation. commandPromptSHA256 is the SHA-256 of the command prompt's template (Prompts.baseCommandPrompt, UTF-8), so both apps send the same text.",
